.TH GGAZE 1 "2026-09-23" "ggaze 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ggaze \- fast native image viewer for culling camera shoots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ggaze
[\fIFILE\fR... | \fIFOLDER\fR] [\fI--version\fR] [\fI--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ggaze (GTK Gaze) is a small, fast, native image viewer for Fedora Linux,
written in C with GTK4. It opens a file or folder, shows a thumbnail grid,
and lets you flip through the shoot with vi-style keys, check EXIF, trash
rejects, and move on. No library, no database, no sidecars.
.PP
A single
.I FILE
opens in the large view with its folder as the navigator; a
.I FOLDER
opens as a thumbnail grid. Several
.I FILE
arguments (or a multi-file drop onto the window) open the first one's
folder in the grid with that file selected. The first argument decides the
folder and the remaining ones are ignored beyond asking for the grid: a
folder given first opens that folder itself, and a first argument that does
not exist, is not an image, is a hidden dotfile (never listed), or is a RAW
sidecar hidden by the
.B Hide RAW sidecars
preference opens its folder on the first image with the status line saying
why. A single
.I FILE
in any of those cases is reported the same way.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B h / l / Left / Right
Previous / next image
.TP
.B Enter / Esc
Grid \[ua] large view / contextual back
.TP
.B i
Info overlay (EXIF)
.TP
.B d / D
Trash to .Trash (undoable) / permanent delete
.TP
.B u
Undo last trash or delete
.TP
.B v / V / Ctrl+a
Toggle mark / range mark / mark all
.TP
.B m
Move marked images to a destination popup
.TP
.B e
Open in an external program popup
.TP
.B !
Run a shell script popup
.TP
.B a
GEGL edit panel (optional): presets, crop, straighten, rotate, save, revert;
a key-hint bar under the image lists the live keys
.TP
.B 1 \- 8
Toggle preset N (only while the edit panel is open)
.TP
.B c / r / [ / ]
Crop / straighten / rotate 90\[de] counter-clockwise / clockwise (open the
edit panel first). Crop: h j k l move, Shift+h j k l grow and Ctrl+h j k l
shrink that side, a cycles the aspect; straighten: h / l nudge, a auto-crop;
Enter applies, Esc cancels
.TP
.B s / x
Save an edited copy (never the original) / revert every edit (edit panel
open). Esc closes the panel and keeps the edit
.TP
.B f / S
Fullscreen / slideshow
.TP
.B t
Toggle grid \[ua] large
.TP
.B + / - / 0
Zoom in / out / fit \[<>] 100% (large) or grow / shrink / reset thumbnails
(grid)
.TP
.B o
Open file/folder dialog
.TP
.B ?
Shortcuts overlay
.TP
.B q
Quit
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/
freedesktop thumbnail cache (shared with other compliant apps)
.TP
.I .Trash/
Local trash folder beside the images (recoverable, not the system trash)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR feh (1),
.BR nsxiv (1),
.BR gthumb (1)